  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Monday)\nIssued at 1022 PM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nFast moving wave will drop southeastward across the central CONUS\ndownstream of the amplifying western CONUS ridge. The associated\ncold front will pass the across the area Wednesday and likely\nremain dry with a period of gusty winds through the day.\nTemperatures will warm quickly ahead of the front and provide\nanother day of well above normal temperatures.\n\nPattern aloft becomes more amplified by Thursday with a deepening\neastern CONUS trough ushering a reinforcing cold front southward.\nTemperatures locally will be seasonably mild on Thursday with\ncooler air arriving by Friday. A light freeze will be possible\nboth Thursday and Friday night primarily in colder valleys. \n\nUpper ridging is quickly undercut by strengthening southern jet\nstream and an associated shortwave trough moving into the \nsouthwest CONUS by Saturday. Southerly winds and more mild \ntemperatures spread across the forecast area ahead of this wave \nwith increasing rain chances Sunday into Monday as the wave tracks\neastward.",
